WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.717
[MUSIC]

00:00:02.717 --> 00:00:07.319
I remember my first study group,
we were from different continents,

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:12.623
different disciplines, we were a mix of
big corporations and entrepreneurs and

00:00:12.623 --> 00:00:17.860
I thought how will we even find a common
language to define the task at hand.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:22.424
But together, we come back to the most
efficient problem solving that I've

00:00:22.424 --> 00:00:26.419
ever experienced and this continued
with every new study group and

00:00:26.419 --> 00:00:30.010
in every discussion as
the program went along.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:33.783
&gt;&gt; When you're talking about Cohort of
some of the most impressive executives all

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:37.895
around the world, they all bring different
capabilities, different experiences,

00:00:37.895 --> 00:00:41.910
different approaches, different
culture to problems or situations.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.820
And that bond with those classmates was
probably the most unexpected thing.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.925
&gt;&gt; You get to interact with
such a diverse population and

00:00:48.925 --> 00:00:53.760
I don't just mean in gender and ethnicity,
although yes, that is part of it.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.360
But culturally and industry,

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.660
I got exposed to industries I had
never been exposed to at STP and

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.860
I also got exposed to
private companies to NGOs and

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:11.960
unless you are intentionally switching
industries in your career you,

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:15.267
we don't often get that opportunity.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:19.724
&gt;&gt; It was really the network and the
strength of that network that came out of

00:01:19.724 --> 00:01:25.079
the program and the lifelong relationships
that you build coming out of that program.

00:01:25.079 --> 00:01:28.655
&gt;&gt; Having that that expanded
support network of both men and

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:33.349
women in leadership positions across
different industries, globally,

00:01:33.349 --> 00:01:37.742
has made me better prepared for
both what I'm doing in my role today and

00:01:37.742 --> 00:01:40.669
I think what I'm going to
be doing in the future.

00:01:40.669 --> 00:01:49.411
[MUSIC]

